  "body": "Copying from https://github.com/w3c/preload/issues/82\r\n\r\nAs pointed out in the review of w3c/web-platform-tests#4316, currently there's no tight definition of what the UA should do:\r\n\r\n* When the preload link's link element is removed from a document.\r\n* When the preload link is changed or removed on a link element that is already in a Document.\r\n\r\nIMO it makes sense for the UA to abort the request if it's in flight. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#abort-the-image-request can serve as a precedent.",
